    <string name="wizard_acesso_nota">It is the most sensitive permission in the app: with it the agent reads the screen and interacts. You can turn it off at any time.</string>
    <string name="wizard_acesso_texto">Without the accessibility service the agent neither sees nor touches the screen — it can only send notifications. Turn it on in Settings → Accessibility → Cachalote.</string>
    <string name="wizard_acesso_titulo">Give the agent eyes and fingers</string>
    <string name="wizard_bemvindo_p1">The agent talks to you in the chat and works in turns: it sees the screen, taps, types and runs commands.</string>
    <string name="wizard_bemvindo_p2">Outside the allowed areas every command asks for your approval on the phone — and is logged.</string>
    <string name="wizard_bemvindo_p3">Your prompts and attached images go to the provider API; nothing else leaves on the app\'s own initiative.</string>
    <string name="wizard_bemvindo_texto">Cachalote runs the DeepSeek Harness agent inside this phone. In the next pages you choose how it runs, give it access to the screen and set your provider key. It takes two minutes.</string>
    <string name="wizard_bemvindo_titulo">Welcome to Cachalote</string>
    <string name="wizard_chave_texto">It is how the agent talks to DeepSeek. Paste it here and the daemon stores it.</string>
    <string name="wizard_chave_titulo">Your provider key</string>
    <string name="wizard_comecar">Start chatting</string>
    <string name="wizard_continuar">Continue</string>
    <string name="wizard_ja_configurado">I already have everything set up</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_detectado_nada">I found neither root nor Shizuku — the embedded mode works right away.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_detectado_root">I found root on this phone — it is the most capable option.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_detectado_shizuku">I found Shizuku running — you can do almost everything without root.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_embutido">Nothing (engine inside the app)</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_embutido_detalhe">The engine runs as part of the app: the safest option, needing neither root nor Shizuku. It downloads the kernel on first use (~160 MB).</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_embutido_risco">The Android sandbox is the limit: the agent cannot leave the app, and there is no root bash.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_escolhido">chosen</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_indisponivel">not available on this phone</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_root">With root (Magisk)</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_root_detalhe">The agent runs as root: it can run commands, install things and touch everything the phone allows.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_root_risco">⚠ Android does not enforce the DSH sandbox here: what stops a command outside the workspace is the approval you give — not the system. The app installs the engine on this phone (~600 MB); Magisk has to allow `su`.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_shizuku">With Shizuku (no root)</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_shizuku_detalhe">The daemon lives in /data/local/tmp and runs as the shell user (uid 2000). Enough to see and touch the screen, notifications and the virtual screen.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_shizuku_risco">No root: it does not reach other apps\' data or system areas. The app installs the engine on this phone (~600 MB); Shizuku has to be running and allow access.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_texto">This decides what the agent can do — and how much the operating system restrains it. You can change it later in Settings → Engine.</string>
    <string name="wizard_modo_titulo">How should the engine run?</string>
